data.content:
In .NET 10, `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded its dependency from **Microsoft.OpenApi v1.x to v2.x**, which targets OpenAPI v3.1 / JSON Schema 2020-12. Here are the breaking changes and fixes:

## 1. `OpenApiString` / `OpenApiAny` types removed

The `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace is gone. `Example` is now a `JsonNode`.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After (.NET 10)
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

## 2. `OpenApiResponse` → response dictionary changes

`operation.Responses` is now a `Dictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>` (no longer `OpenApiResponses` subclass). `TryAdd` still works, but ensure you're using the new namespace:

```csharp
// This still compiles — no change needed
operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });
```

## 3. `OpenApiReference.Type` → `ReferenceType` replaced

`ReferenceType` moved and `OpenApiReference` now uses a `string`-based type:

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }

// After (.NET 10)
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
// If ReferenceType is missing, use the string overload:
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Id = "oauth2" }
```

In OpenApi v2, the `Type` on `OpenApiSecurityScheme` can be inferred from context. If `ReferenceType` still exists in your version, this compiles as-is.

## 4. `schema.Nullable` removed

OpenAPI 3.1 expresses nullability via the `type` array, not a `nullable` boolean.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After (.NET 10) — to make something nullable you ADD "null" to Type:
// To ensure NOT nullable, remove it:
property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

`Type` is now a `JsonSchemaType` flags enum where `Null` is a flag.

## Full corrected code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of changes:**
| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `new OpenApiString("x")` | `JsonValue.Create("x")` |
| `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` | `using System.Text.Json.Nodes` |
| `schema.Nullable = false` | `schema.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null` |
